      "text": "To find the number of minutes required to print 200 pages, we can set up a proportion. Let $m$ represent the unknown number of minutes.\n\nSince the printer prints 17 pages per minute, we have:\n$$\n\\frac{17}{\\text{minutes}} = \\frac{200}{m}\n$$\n\nCross-multiplying and solving for $m$, we get:\n$$\n17m = 200 \\cdot {\\text{minutes}}\n$$\n$$\nm = \\frac{200}{17}\n$$\n\nConverting to a mixed number, we get:\n$$\nm \\approx 11.76\n$$\n\nSince we are asked to express the answer to the nearest whole number, our answer is:\n$$\n\\boxed{12} \\text{ minutes}\n$$",
